>>__ load "simpLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `del_split`

``` hol4
simpLib.del_split : string -> simpLib.simpset -> simpLib.simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Removes split loopers from a simpset.

`del_split name ss` removes the loopers `split name` and `split_asm name`
added by `add_split`. If `name` itself begins with `split ` or
`split_asm `, only that looper is removed. Rules with the persistent
`[split]` attribute are not affected; use `ExclX ("split:" ^ name)` to
exclude one from a simplifier call, or `splitLib.exclude_split` to
retract it.

### Failure

Never fails. If there is no matching looper, `ss` is returned.

### Example

``` hol4
>>_ val ss = simpLib.add_split (splitLib.type_split_of “:'a option”)
     boolSimps.bool_ss;
>>_ val ss' = simpLib.del_split "option$option_CASE" ss;
```

### See also

[`simpLib.add_split`](#simpLib.add_split),
[`splitLib.exclude_split`](#splitLib.exclude_split),
[`simpLib.ExclX`](#simpLib.ExclX).
